## 15. Codify lifecycle

Every task follows the same evidence loop:

1. Claim a conflict-free eligible task with a named agent and bounded lease.
2. Open the revisioned work packet and use graph context, survey, impact, why, and recall before editing.
3. Start the task and implement only its declared acceptance criteria and paths.
4. Update progress with novel evidence and record durable decisions or constraints.
5. Run test impact, review, guard, and the focused verification command.
6. Snapshot with task attribution.
7. In parallel Prod semantics, mark source-complete work implemented only when graph evidence exists; mark done only when executable qualification passes.
8. Trace task to symbols, touched files, commits, memories, and evidence.
9. Hand off exact done, next, and blocked state before changing owner or ending a session.

No process exit, status declaration, fixture-only green result, or generated Markdown is completion evidence.

## 16. Release proof

The primary journey begins with a real non-Discord channel message. Keith resumes the same durable session through Web or ACP, uses an explicitly connected application, opens Keith Computer, and lets the user observe and take control. The user records a task, corrects the compiled recipe, replays it, publishes it as a skill, and invokes it from a channel.

The same release then exposes a deliberate harness defect. Keith captures the failed trace, attributes the harness cause, creates several candidates, evaluates them against search and inaccessible held-out tasks, promotes a non-regressing winner through the real self-evolution path, reruns successfully, and restores the prior harness in one action.

The release remains in progress if any named platform lacks credentialed proof, any authority boundary can be widened, any profile can cross into another, any credential leaks, any computer input can race, any recording retains a secret, any evaluator can be influenced by a candidate, any external action can be blindly replayed, or any promoted change cannot be reversed.
